omarchy-mac (omacom/omarchy-mac-pkgs): cutout entries for the MacBook Pro 14-inch OLED, M5 Pro
(apple,k114s). Its boot framebuffer is 3024x1986 and the loader sets asahi,show-notch, so no entry
of the shipped list matches and the bar has no notch floor. top = 96 physical rows is DERIVED, not
measured: the K116s (same 254.6 ppi dot pitch in the ADT, "identical node for node") has a
96-pixel notch upstream-reported (3472x2266 shown, 3472x2170 hidden). Measure it on the panel before
sending this upstream (tests/hardware/k114s-platform-data-check.sh). A mode with the notch hidden
needs no entry.

Two lines, one for each name the panel can have:
  - connector "eDP": the panel once the display coprocessor (or the r3a internal-panel patch) names it
    eDP-1. This is the line for upstream.
  - connector "Unknown-1": LOCAL ONLY, not for upstream. Until then the screen is the boot framebuffer
    (simpledrm), which Hyprland names Unknown-1 (agent-run, hyprctl monitors: "Unknown-1 3024x1986"),
    and the cutout matches on a connector-name prefix. Anything else Hyprland calls Unknown-1 at exactly
    3024x1986 would get the floor too. Delete this line when the panel is eDP-1.
See docs/platform-data.md.

